# Vendored conformance fixtures are pinned, byte-for-byte copies of upstream
# files (see fixtures/vendor/README.md and provenance.json for recorded
# sizes and SHA-256 digests). Git's default line-ending conversion would
# rewrite LF to CRLF for anything it guesses is text on a Windows checkout,
# silently corrupting those pinned bytes and breaking provenance
# verification. Mark the whole tree binary so every checkout gets the exact
# bytes regardless of platform.
packages/c2pa_testkit/test/fixtures/vendor/** -text
